            <div xml:id="d1068">

                <pb facs="0934" n="922" xml:id="pg922"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">838.51/4107a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Haiti</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Sparks</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-11-01T17:00:00-05:00">November 1, 1940—5
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>177. Minister Lescot was told in an informal conference that the Department would
                    interpose no objections if the Haitian Government should present a request to
                    the Foreign Bondholders Protective Council for a reduction in the interest rate
                    on Haiti’s dollar bonds from 6 percent to 4 percent.</p>
                <p>Lescot indicated that he would inform his Government of this fact with a
                    recommendation that a statement be prepared by his Government, presumably with
                    the assistance of the Fiscal Representative, for submission to the Council.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
